      "content": "New arrivals in gentrifying areas often possess higher levels of education, white-collar employment, and are generally more affluent. Conversely, the long-term, original residents frequently have lower-to-middle incomes and may be working-class or minority groups. This demographic shift often leads to displacement, where the original, lower-income community is priced out by rising costs. Essentially, the neighborhood experiences a change from a working-class to a more affluent demographic.",
